From 45e32b200fb4bf8648f9d5f4c08e97a0ca52cd04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kartikya Motwani <kartikya@local>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 17:27:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Angel One SmartAPI as an optional live price feed
 (data-only, no static IP needed)

Adds app/services/angel_feed.py and AngelLiveFeed (bot_runner.py),
selectable via a new PRICE_FEED env var ("yahoo", the existing
default, or "angel"). Nothing changes for anyone who doesn't set this
- YahooLiveFeed stays the default.

Why this is possible on Render's free tier: Angel One's static-IP
requirement (per their own docs) only applies to order/GTT endpoints
- ltpData() and the instrument master are market-data endpoints and
work from any IP. Since the bot only ever paper-trades (PaperBroker,
no real orders sent to Angel One), this only needs the data side.

What's new:
- app/services/angel_feed.py: downloads and disk-caches Angel's
  instrument master JSON (24h TTL) to build a symbol -> (tradingsymbol,
  token) map for NSE equities, since Angel's LTP API needs a numeric
  symboltoken rather than a plain ticker. get_angel_ltp() mirrors
  price_feed.get_live_price()'s exact return shape and 60s cache
  behavior, so it's a drop-in. Session login is lazy and reused; a
  failed call triggers one re-login retry (Angel force-logs-out
  sessions daily).
- AngelLiveFeed class in bot_runner.py: same .prices/.get_price()
  interface as YahooLiveFeed (this was literally already anticipated -
  YahooLiveFeed's own docstring says "same interface as
  SimulatedFeed/AngelLiveFeed", it just never got built until now).
- settings.PRICE_FEED (config.py), default "yahoo".

Tested: instrument-master parsing and token lookup verified against
realistic mocked rows (correctly filters to NSE equity segment,
resolves bare symbols, raises a clear error for unknown ones). All
17 existing tests still pass. NOT tested against Angel One's real
servers - this sandbox has no network access to angelone.in domains,
so the actual login + ltpData call needs to be verified live before
relying on it. Recommend: set PRICE_FEED=angel alongside the existing
ANGEL_* credentials on Render, watch the logs for "Angel One data
session established" and any errors on the first few ticks, and keep
PRICE_FEED unset (defaults to yahoo) as the safe fallback if anything
looks wrong.
